 "details": {
  "title": "I’m in the Mood for Love",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet, set on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement, which follows Rod Stewart’s record three half steps down, in D (E for the trumpet), concert C♯4 to E5. It plays in that guitar track’s time, about 87. It keeps Rod’s short phrases; C♯ holds over the band’s F diminished 7, where the book’s C would rub; and where the band moves to B7♭9 under the tune’s long D it lets the D go before the chord comes. The eight bars where the record’s horn plays the A while Rod rests are the trumpet’s too. A short line leads in, and the tag sets the last phrase over the band’s held A chords, lands on D and turns to G minor before the last F♯.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Song",
    "Jimmy McHugh and Dorothy Fields (1935)"
   ],
   [
    "Line",
    "The tune from the lead sheet, in the form and chords of Rod Stewart’s record; the tag is new"
   ],
   [
    "Key",
    "D major concert (E for the trumpet)"
   ],
   [
    "Form",
    "Intro, A A bridge A, the horn’s A, bridge, A, tag"
   ],
   [
    "Plays with",
    "The guitar track on the Fret Finder page (mood-guitar.mp3), 3:05"
   ],
   [
    "Bars",
    "The same numbers as the Fret Finder page"
   ]
  ]
 }
